          "id": "44d6102eb6373ab99b9a3d395acf2fd81c8e663b",
          "message": "docs(research): cloud-deploy architecture + secure-defaults design for sq-3vjdr [OPUS-4.8] (#2313)\n\nDesign record for the maintainer-requested epic sq-3vjdr (1-click cloud deploy\nof the sparq servers). Makes the architecture + security decisions once so each\nchild (sq-17rgw/zcou4/agolp/sos84/0d744/dwame/44ga1 + sq-lmz40) is implementable:\n\n- Shared substrate: the merged sq-fvzi6 GHCR sparq-server image (port 3030,\n  /health) + the sq-lmz40 native LWS image (port 3000, /livez+/readyz), with the\n  verified image contracts (env, ports, health, non-root).\n- Secure defaults R1-R9 as copy-into-each-template rules. KEY: sparq-server is\n  open-by-default at the IMAGE layer (bakes SPARQ_ALLOW_REMOTE=1, no auth), so\n  auth-ON / no-anonymous-write is enforced at the TEMPLATE layer; LWS is\n  already fail-closed.\n- Per-provider approach (AWS Fargate+EC2, Azure Container Apps, GCP Cloud Run,\n  multi-cloud Terraform, Helm, PaaS) + the CI-smoke contract (non-gating).\n- Child bead -> section map with acceptance criteria; deps wired\n  (sq-lmz40 -> provider children -> site). Disjoint file-areas.\n\nDesigned-only: no template implemented here. Open questions for the maintainer\nin section 6 (GHCR org ref, LWS external IdP, no standing cloud spend in CI).\n\nCo-authored-by: GPT-5.6 <noreply@openai.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-15T12:52:35Z",
