          "id": "baa6cf0c4e09a479c111cac6a6f3626ca93f89e0",
          "message": "feat(deploy): GCP Cloud Run one-click for sq-agolp [SONNET] (#2316)\n\n* feat(deploy): GCP Cloud Run one-click for sq-agolp [SONNET]\n\nDelivers deploy/gcp/** (disjoint from deploy/aws/ and deploy/paas/):\n\n- deploy/gcp/sparq-server.yaml  Cloud Run Knative/serving.knative.dev/v1 spec\n  for sparq-server (port 3030, /health probes, min-instances=1).\n  SPARQ_AUTH_TOKEN wired from GCP Secret Manager via secretKeyRef (R4).\n  Dedicated sparq-server-sa with secretAccessor on own secret only (R5).\n\n- deploy/gcp/sparq-lws.yaml  Cloud Run spec for sparq-lws-core (port 3000,\n  /livez liveness + /readyz readiness, min-instances=1, max-instances=1\n  pending sq-lmz40 Redis DPoP replay). Activates once sq-lmz40 ships.\n  Fail-closed by image design (R2).\n\n- deploy/gcp/README.md  Prerequisites, gcloud one-liner, \"Run on Google\n  Cloud\" button, verify-deploy commands, decisions table. Secure-defaults\n  notice (R1/R2/R3/R4/R5/R7/R8/R9). Under 120 lines of content prose\n  (not a crate README; readme-template gate does not apply here).\n\nSecure-defaults satisfied: R1 auth ON via secretKeyRef; R2 fail-closed LWS;\nR3 automatic Cloud Run HTTPS; R4 no plaintext secret anywhere; R5 dedicated\nSA; R7 startup+liveness probes; R8 non-root distroless image unchanged; R9\nhonest open-by-default caveat in every header and the README.\n\nStatic acceptance: YAML valid (python yaml.safe_load); Knative v1 structural\ncheck passes; secretKeyRef confirmed; secret-literal grep clean; typos gate\nclean. gcloud --dry-run unavailable (not installed); marked documented-\nuntested on live Cloud Run deploy; validate on first CI run.\n\nNo workflow changes; ci-summary gate aggregator intact; path-filter skips\nRust jobs (no crates/ changes). No new gating check added.\n\n[SONNET-4.6] sq-agolp\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(deploy): harden GCP Cloud Run manifests [GPT-5.6]\n\nCo-Authored-By: GPT-5.6 <noreply@openai.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: GPT-5.6 <noreply@openai.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
